    "https://www.neiu.edu/assistant-professor-social-work": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Social Work",
      "description": "Assistant Professor - Social Work | NEIU Skip to main content Join us at NEIU's Graduate Open House on Oct. 20. Learn more . Admissions Learn About NEIU Visit Us Our Programs Requirements Admitted Students Your Success Profile Graduate Studies Continue Your Education Parents and Family Resources One Stop Center Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Tuition Information Fees Information Calculating Your Net Cost Scholarship Opportunities Scholarship Listing Applying for Federal & State Assistance Documents Summer Financial Aid Resources Financial Aid Forms & Documents Resources Applying for Student Loans Student Employment Opportunities Student Payment Services Academics Taking Classes Class Schedules & Registration Academic Calendar Advising Center Majors, Minors, Graduate Programs & Certificates University Core Curriculum / General Education Community & Professional Education Academic Units All Academic Departments College of Arts & Sciences College of Business & Technology Daniel L. Goodwin College of Education College of Graduate Studies & Research Nontraditional Degree Programs Carruthers Center for Inner City Studies El Centro University Center of Lake County Center for College Access and Success First-Year Experience Our Centers and Programs Opportunities International Programs Research Resources McNair Scholars University Honors Program Student Center for Science Engagement Intensive English Program Resources Center for Teaching and Learning Registrar Services Transcripts Academic Catalog Student Achievement Information Assessment University Life Things To Do Academic Calendar Campus Recreation Student Union Arts at Northeastern Box Office Student Leadership & Organizations Support Learning Success Center TRIO Student Support Services Project Success Proyecto Pa’Lante Student Affairs Dean of Students Advising Center Student Success and Retention Services All Student Resources Student Counseling Services Career Development Student Health Services Student Disability Services Veterans Services Parking University Police Bookstore Child Care Center Technology Services Event & Conference Services Immigration Enforcement Actions Resources Library Pedroso Center Undocumented Student Resources Black Student Success Committee Title IX New Student Resources Guide BIG Center Living on Campus Student Housing Living Learning Communities Alumni & Giving Alumni Your Membership Alumni Events Office of Alumni Relations Giving Giving Opportunities Impact of Your Gift Scholarships Foundation Meet Our Staff Transforming Lives About Who We Are Northeastern News Facts & Distinctions Community & Visitor Guide Northeastern History Mission, Vision and Values Strategic Planning Accreditation Office of Institutional Research & Assessment Our Leadership University Leadership President Executive Team Shared Governance Board of Trustees Employment Working Here Resources Brand Guide Complaints Northeastern Neighbors Legal Menu Audience Menu Audience Placeholder What can we help you find? Menu Actions Menu Actions Give Now Request Info Visit Apply Home — \n                                Assistant Professor - Social Work Assistant Professor - Social Work Job Summary: The Department of Social Work at Northeastern Illinois University (NEIU) invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor position beginning in January or August 2027. Job Description: The successful candidate will teach undergraduate and graduate social work courses, with primary teaching responsibilities in the Bachelor of Social Work (BSW) program. The position includes responsibility for coordinating and providing leadership for the BSW research curriculum while collaborating with faculty across the BSW and MSW programs to promote continuity in research education. Because of the collaborative nature of the department and curricular needs, candidates should also be prepared to teach practice courses in the BSW curriculum. Additional responsibilities include advising students, maintaining an active program of scholarship, and providing service to the department, college, university, and profession. The Department of Social Work values collaborative teaching, engaged scholarship, community partnerships, and the preparation of ethical social workers who advance social and economic justice. We seek colleagues who are committed to student success and who view teaching, scholarship, and service as mutually reinforcing aspects of academic life. Minimal Qualifications: A doctorate in social work or a closely related field (ABD candidates will be considered if all degree requirements are completed before the appointment begins). An MSW from a CSWE-accredited program. At least two years of post-MSW practice experience. Preferred Qualifications : Preference will be given to candidates who demonstrate: Evidence of effective teaching or strong potential for teaching effectiveness in higher education. Experience coordinating, developing, or providing leadership for a social work research curriculum. An active or developing scholarly agenda. Evidence of service and the ability to contribute to the department, university, profession, and community. Experience creating inclusive learning environments and supporting the success of students from diverse backgrounds. Candidates should address the following in their application: Experience teaching, mentoring, and supporting students from historically underserved and minoritized communities, including Latinx, African American, and other diverse student populations. A willingness to reflect upon and continuously strengthen instructional, mentoring, and classroom practices to promote student success. Experience integrating equity, inclusion, and social justice into teaching and learning. Experience using culturally responsive and inclusive teaching practices that connect course content to students' lived experiences and communities. Demonstrated ability to use reflective or data-informed teaching practices to identify and address equity gaps within courses and classrooms. Application Materials: Applicants should submit the following as one PDF file through the NEIU Workday application system : Letter of application addressing the minimum and preferred qualifications. Curriculum vitae. Transcripts. Statement of teaching philosophy. Research statement describing the candidate's scholarly agenda. One or two samples of scholarly writing or publications. Three letters of reference, including at least one addressing teaching effectiveness. Please note that all candidates must be able and willing to teach face-to-face courses, in some cases at multiple NEIU campuses, as well as hold office hours face-to-face on-campus. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. This position requires a background check. Salary Range 65,000-68,000 Benefits University employees may be eligible for a variety of State of Illinois benefits. These benefits are administered through the Illinois Department of Central Management Services (CMS). Please visit our Employee Benefits page to learn more about our comprehensive benefits package, including health, dental, and vision benefits, sick and vacation days, and participation in the State Universities Retirement System. Northeastern Illinois University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer and invites applications from Women, Minorities, Veterans and Persons with Disabilities, as well as other qualified individuals. Northeastern Illinois University's positions are contingent upon the University's receipt of its State of Illinois appropriation. Our Mission is You Request Information Plan a Visit Apply Now Footer Menu 1 Footer Menu 1 Online Learning Academic Calendar NEIUPort Maps & Directions Housing Events Employment Directory Community Library Main Campus 5500 North St. Louis Avenue Chicago, IL 60625 (773) 583-4050 Carruthers Center 700 East Oakwood Blvd. Chicago, IL 60625 (773) 268-7500 El Centro 3390 North Avondale Ave. Chicago, IL 60618 (773) 442-4080 University Center 1200 University Center Drive, Room 220B Grayslake, IL 60030 (847) 665-4000 Footer bottom Footer bottom Take a Virtual Tour Give to NEIU © 2022 Northeastern Illinois University | Legal | Login Also of Interest High-Quality Access-Driven Online Credit Courses Student Services and Support in Illinois University Campus Virtual Tour ↑"
    },
    "https://www.neiu.edu/career-instructorinternship-coordinator": {
      "title": "Career Instructor/Internship Coordinator",
      "description": "Career Instructor/Internship Coordinator | NEIU Skip to main content Join us at NEIU's Graduate Open House on Oct. 20. Learn more . Admissions Learn About NEIU Visit Us Our Programs Requirements Admitted Students Your Success Profile Graduate Studies Continue Your Education Parents and Family Resources One Stop Center Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Tuition Information Fees Information Calculating Your Net Cost Scholarship Opportunities Scholarship Listing Applying for Federal & State Assistance Documents Summer Financial Aid Resources Financial Aid Forms & Documents Resources Applying for Student Loans Student Employment Opportunities Student Payment Services Academics Taking Classes Class Schedules & Registration Academic Calendar Advising Center Majors, Minors, Graduate Programs & Certificates University Core Curriculum / General Education Community & Professional Education Academic Units All Academic Departments College of Arts & Sciences College of Business & Technology Daniel L. Goodwin College of Education College of Graduate Studies & Research Nontraditional Degree Programs Carruthers Center for Inner City Studies El Centro University Center of Lake County Center for College Access and Success First-Year Experience Our Centers and Programs Opportunities International Programs Research Resources McNair Scholars University Honors Program Student Center for Science Engagement Intensive English Program Resources Center for Teaching and Learning Registrar Services Transcripts Academic Catalog Student Achievement Information Assessment University Life Things To Do Academic Calendar Campus Recreation Student Union Arts at Northeastern Box Office Student Leadership & Organizations Support Learning Success Center TRIO Student Support Services Project Success Proyecto Pa’Lante Student Affairs Dean of Students Advising Center Student Success and Retention Services All Student Resources Student Counseling Services Career Development Student Health Services Student Disability Services Veterans Services Parking University Police Bookstore Child Care Center Technology Services Event & Conference Services Immigration Enforcement Actions Resources Library Pedroso Center Undocumented Student Resources Black Student Success Committee Title IX New Student Resources Guide BIG Center Living on Campus Student Housing Living Learning Communities Alumni & Giving Alumni Your Membership Alumni Events Office of Alumni Relations Giving Giving Opportunities Impact of Your Gift Scholarships Foundation Meet Our Staff Transforming Lives About Who We Are Northeastern News Facts & Distinctions Community & Visitor Guide Northeastern History Mission, Vision and Values Strategic Planning Accreditation Office of Institutional Research & Assessment Our Leadership University Leadership President Executive Team Shared Governance Board of Trustees Employment Working Here Resources Brand Guide Complaints Northeastern Neighbors Legal Menu Audience Menu Audience Placeholder What can we help you find? Menu Actions Menu Actions Give Now Request Info Visit Apply Home — \n                                Career Instructor/Internship Coordinator Career Instructor/Internship Coordinator The College of Business and Technology at Northeastern Illinois University (NEIU) invites applications for one full-time instructor focused on career development in the College of Business & Technology. This position will start in late Fall 2026, pending final funding approval. Minimum Requirements Applicants should have a Masters degree in a business or computer-science related field. The successful candidate should be able to teach traditional courses as well as seminars. They should also have the personal engagement skills necessary to engage in service activities related to career. Demonstrated potential for excellence in teaching and research is required. Relevant business experience will also be helpful. Job Responsibilities This position is responsible for delivering the equivalent of 8 courses per year and service activities. Assignments may include (a) traditional courses (career); (b) short career-related seminars; (c) work with students individually; (d) engage City of Chicago industry to develop new internship opportunities for students taking the internship course; and (e) data analysis and reporting of results. This position will reside in the Department of Management and Marketing but will be delegated to work with the Associate Dean’s career team. Application Send an application letter, vitae, copy of transcripts, the names and contact information of at least three professional references, most recent student evaluations, and sample research work electronically (via email: mm-car@neiu.edu ) to Dr. Qiumei Xu, Associate Dean, College of Business and Technology, Northeastern Illinois University, 5500 North St. Louis Avenue, Chicago, IL 60625. While unofficial transcripts are accepted, official transcripts for all earned degrees are required of candidates selected for final interviews. The position also requires a background check. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Salary and Benefits The salary range for this position is $60,000 - $70,000. University employees may be eligible for a variety of State of Illinois benefits. These benefits are administered through the Illinois Department of Central Management Service (CMS). Please visit our Employee Benefits page to learn more about our comprehensive benefits package including health, dental, and vision benefits, sick and vacation days, and participation in the State Universities Retirement System. About NEIU Founded in 1867, Northeastern Illinois University enrolls about 5,500 students through the College of Arts and Sciences, the Daniel L. Goodwin College of Education, the College of Business and Technology and the College of Graduate Studies and Research. Northeastern is regarded as the most diverse public comprehensive university in the Midwest and is designated by the U.S. Department of Education as a Hispanic-Serving Institution. NEIU offers more than 40 undergraduate degree and certificate programs and more than 50 graduate degree, certificate, licensure and endorsement programs. NEIU’s Main Campus is located on 67 acres in a residential area on the Northwest Side of Chicago. The University has three additional locations in the metropolitan area: the Jacob H. Carruthers Center for Inner City Studies, El Centro and the Center for College Access and Success. NEIU also is a founding member of the University Center of Lake County consortium campus in suburban Lake County, north of Chicago. Read more about us at www.neiu.edu . Our Mission is You Request Information Plan a Visit Apply Now Footer Menu 1 Footer Menu 1 Online Learning Academic Calendar NEIUPort Maps & Directions Housing Events Employment Directory Community Library Main Campus 5500 North St. Louis Avenue Chicago, IL 60625 (773) 583-4050 Carruthers Center 700 East Oakwood Blvd. Chicago, IL 60625 (773) 268-7500 El Centro 3390 North Avondale Ave. Chicago, IL 60618 (773) 442-4080 University Center 1200 University Center Drive, Room 220B Grayslake, IL 60030 (847) 665-4000 Footer bottom Footer bottom Take a Virtual Tour Give to NEIU © 2022 Northeastern Illinois University | Legal | Login Also of Interest High-Quality Access-Driven Online Credit Courses Student Services and Support in Illinois University Campus Virtual Tour ↑"
    },
    "https://www.neiu.edu/entrepreneurship-instructor": {
      "title": "Entrepreneurship Instructor",
      "description": "Entrepreneurship Instructor | NEIU Skip to main content Join us at NEIU's Graduate Open House on Oct. 20. Learn more . Admissions Learn About NEIU Visit Us Our Programs Requirements Admitted Students Your Success Profile Graduate Studies Continue Your Education Parents and Family Resources One Stop Center Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Tuition Information Fees Information Calculating Your Net Cost Scholarship Opportunities Scholarship Listing Applying for Federal & State Assistance Documents Summer Financial Aid Resources Financial Aid Forms & Documents Resources Applying for Student Loans Student Employment Opportunities Student Payment Services Academics Taking Classes Class Schedules & Registration Academic Calendar Advising Center Majors, Minors, Graduate Programs & Certificates University Core Curriculum / General Education Community & Professional Education Academic Units All Academic Departments College of Arts & Sciences College of Business & Technology Daniel L. Goodwin College of Education College of Graduate Studies & Research Nontraditional Degree Programs Carruthers Center for Inner City Studies El Centro University Center of Lake County Center for College Access and Success First-Year Experience Our Centers and Programs Opportunities International Programs Research Resources McNair Scholars University Honors Program Student Center for Science Engagement Intensive English Program Resources Center for Teaching and Learning Registrar Services Transcripts Academic Catalog Student Achievement Information Assessment University Life Things To Do Academic Calendar Campus Recreation Student Union Arts at Northeastern Box Office Student Leadership & Organizations Support Learning Success Center TRIO Student Support Services Project Success Proyecto Pa’Lante Student Affairs Dean of Students Advising Center Student Success and Retention Services All Student Resources Student Counseling Services Career Development Student Health Services Student Disability Services Veterans Services Parking University Police Bookstore Child Care Center Technology Services Event & Conference Services Immigration Enforcement Actions Resources Library Pedroso Center Undocumented Student Resources Black Student Success Committee Title IX New Student Resources Guide BIG Center Living on Campus Student Housing Living Learning Communities Alumni & Giving Alumni Your Membership Alumni Events Office of Alumni Relations Giving Giving Opportunities Impact of Your Gift Scholarships Foundation Meet Our Staff Transforming Lives About Who We Are Northeastern News Facts & Distinctions Community & Visitor Guide Northeastern History Mission, Vision and Values Strategic Planning Accreditation Office of Institutional Research & Assessment Our Leadership University Leadership President Executive Team Shared Governance Board of Trustees Employment Working Here Resources Brand Guide Complaints Northeastern Neighbors Legal Menu Audience Menu Audience Placeholder What can we help you find? Menu Actions Menu Actions Give Now Request Info Visit Apply Home — \n                                Entrepreneurship Instructor Entrepreneurship Instructor The College of Business and Technology at Northeastern Illinois University (NEIU) invites applications for one full-time instructor focused on entrepreneurship and business innovation in the Department of Management. This position will start in late Fall 2026, pending final funding approval. Minimum Requirements Applicants should have a Masters degree (or higher) in a business-related field by the starting date of appointment. This appointment may be converted to tenure-track in the future if the required degrees exist, and appropriate funding is procured. The ideal candidate will also have experience as a founder of a new business or a continuing generation of a family business. The successful candidate should be able to teach traditional undergraduate and graduate courses in the field of entrepreneurship as well as seminar type courses through the NEIU CBT Business Innovation and Growth (BIG) center. They should also have the personal engagement skills necessary to engage in service activities related to community outreach. Demonstrated potential for excellence in teaching is required. Relevant business experience will also be helpful. Job Responsibilities This position is responsible for delivering the equivalent of 8 courses per year and some service activities. Teaching assignments may include (a) traditional courses (entrepreneurship, small business management, business practicum, business internship); (b) seminars for BIG (“Build Your Own Business”); (c) serve as a thought partner and provide guidance to our BIG founders; (d) develop new curriculum as appropriate for BIG participants, and (e) engage in service activities related to the entrepreneurship enterprise of CBT/BIG. This position reports to the Department Chair of Management and Marketing with a dotted-line report to the Executive Director of the BIG center. Application Send an application letter, vitae, copy of transcripts, the names and contact information of at least three professional references, most recent student evaluations, and sample research work electronically (via email: mm-big@neiu.edu ) to Dr. Charles Funk, Chair, Department of Management and Marketing, College of Business and Technology, Northeastern Illinois University, 5500 North St. Louis Avenue, Chicago, IL 60625. While unofficial transcripts are accepted, official transcripts for all earned degrees are required of candidates selected for final interviews. The position also requires a background check. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Salary and Benefits The salary range for this position is $70,000 - $80,000. University employees may be eligible for a variety of State of Illinois benefits. These benefits are administered through the Illinois Department of Central Management Service (CMS). Please visit our Employee Benefits page to learn more about our comprehensive benefits package including health, dental, and vision benefits, sick and vacation days, and participation in the State Universities Retirement System. About NEIU Founded in 1867, Northeastern Illinois University enrolls about 5,500 students through the College of Arts and Sciences, the Daniel L. Goodwin College of Education, the College of Business and Technology and the College of Graduate Studies and Research. Northeastern is regarded as the most diverse public comprehensive university in the Midwest and is designated by the U.S. Department of Education as a Hispanic-Serving Institution. NEIU offers more than 40 undergraduate degree and certificate programs and more than 50 graduate degree, certificate, licensure and endorsement programs. NEIU’s Main Campus is located on 67 acres in a residential area on the Northwest Side of Chicago. The University has three additional locations in the metropolitan area: the Jacob H. Carruthers Center for Inner City Studies, El Centro and the Center for College Access and Success. NEIU also is a founding member of the University Center of Lake County consortium campus in suburban Lake County, north of Chicago. Read more about us at www.neiu.edu. Our Mission is You Request Information Plan a Visit Apply Now Footer Menu 1 Footer Menu 1 Online Learning Academic Calendar NEIUPort Maps & Directions Housing Events Employment Directory Community Library Main Campus 5500 North St. Louis Avenue Chicago, IL 60625 (773) 583-4050 Carruthers Center 700 East Oakwood Blvd. Chicago, IL 60625 (773) 268-7500 El Centro 3390 North Avondale Ave. Chicago, IL 60618 (773) 442-4080 University Center 1200 University Center Drive, Room 220B Grayslake, IL 60030 (847) 665-4000 Footer bottom Footer bottom Take a Virtual Tour Give to NEIU © 2022 Northeastern Illinois University | Legal | Login Also of Interest High-Quality Access-Driven Online Credit Courses Student Services and Support in Illinois University Campus Virtual Tour ↑"
