    "https://www.neiu.edu/tenure-track-faculty-assistant-professor-marketing": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Faculty - Assistant Professor in Marketing",
      "description": "Tenure-Track Faculty - Assistant Professor in Marketing | NEIU Skip to main content Join us at NEIU's Graduate Open House on Oct. 20. Learn more . Admissions Learn About NEIU Visit Us Our Programs Requirements Admitted Students Your Success Profile Graduate Studies Continue Your Education Parents and Family Resources One Stop Center Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Tuition Information Fees Information Calculating Your Net Cost Scholarship Opportunities Scholarship Listing Applying for Federal & State Assistance Documents Summer Financial Aid Resources Financial Aid Forms & Documents Resources Applying for Student Loans Student Employment Opportunities Student Payment Services Academics Taking Classes Class Schedules & Registration Academic Calendar Advising Center Majors, Minors, Graduate Programs & Certificates University Core Curriculum / General Education Community & Professional Education Academic Units All Academic Departments College of Arts & Sciences College of Business & Technology Daniel L. Goodwin College of Education College of Graduate Studies & Research Nontraditional Degree Programs Carruthers Center for Inner City Studies El Centro University Center of Lake County Center for College Access and Success First-Year Experience Our Centers and Programs Opportunities International Programs Research Resources McNair Scholars University Honors Program Student Center for Science Engagement Intensive English Program Resources Center for Teaching and Learning Registrar Services Transcripts Academic Catalog Student Achievement Information Assessment University Life Things To Do Academic Calendar Campus Recreation Student Union Arts at Northeastern Box Office Student Leadership & Organizations Support Learning Success Center TRIO Student Support Services Project Success Proyecto Pa’Lante Student Affairs Dean of Students Advising Center Student Success and Retention Services All Student Resources Student Counseling Services Career Development Student Health Services Student Disability Services Veterans Services Parking University Police Bookstore Child Care Center Technology Services Event & Conference Services Immigration Enforcement Actions Resources Library Pedroso Center Undocumented Student Resources Black Student Success Committee Title IX New Student Resources Guide BIG Center Living on Campus Student Housing Living Learning Communities Alumni & Giving Alumni Your Membership Alumni Events Office of Alumni Relations Giving Giving Opportunities Impact of Your Gift Scholarships Foundation Meet Our Staff Transforming Lives About Who We Are Northeastern News Facts & Distinctions Community & Visitor Guide Northeastern History Mission, Vision and Values Strategic Planning Accreditation Office of Institutional Research & Assessment Our Leadership University Leadership President Executive Team Shared Governance Board of Trustees Employment Working Here Resources Brand Guide Complaints Northeastern Neighbors Legal Menu Audience Menu Audience Placeholder What can we help you find? Menu Actions Menu Actions Give Now Request Info Visit Apply Home — \n                                Tenure-Track Faculty - Assistant Professor in Marketing Tenure-Track Faculty - Assistant Professor in Marketing The College of Business and Technology at Northeastern Illinois University (NEIU) invites applications for one tenure-track faculty position at the Assistant Professor rank in Marketing. This position will start in Fall 2027, pending final funding approval. Minimum Requirements Applicants should have received a Ph.D./D.B.A degree in Marketing or a closely related field from an AACSB-accredited school by the starting date of appointment. ABD’s will be considered for a one-year, non-tenure-track initial appointment.  This appointment can be converted to tenure-track if the required degree is completed within the initial year. Qualifications The successful candidate should be able to teach undergraduate and graduate courses in Marketing Research, Marketing Analytics, International Marketing, Personal Selling, Sales Management and other marketing courses in our programs; conduct quality research; and participate in service activities to the NEIU community. Demonstrated potential for excellence in teaching and research is required. Relevant business experience will also be helpful. Application Send an application letter, vitae, copy of transcripts, the names and contact information of at least three professional references, most recent student evaluations, and sample research work electronically (via email: MGT-MKTG@Neiu.edu) to Dr. Charles Funk, Chair, Department of Management and Marketing, College of Business and Technology, Northeastern Illinois University, 5500 North St. Louis Avenue, Chicago, IL 60625. While unofficial transcripts are accepted, official transcripts for all earned degrees are required of candidates selected for final interviews. The position also requires a background check. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. AMA Conference Interviews Members of the search committee will be attending the American Marketing Association Summer Academic Conference, July 24-26, 2026 in Denver, Colorado. We will be conducting informational interviews on-site (in-person) during the conference. Interested candidates should submit their application materials early to be considered for an on-site interview. Please indicate in your cover letter if you plan to attend the conference. Salary and Benefits The salary range for this position is $130,000 - $140,000. University employees may be eligible for a variety of State of Illinois benefits. These benefits are administered through the Illinois Department of Central Management Service (CMS). Please visit our Employee Benefits page to learn more about our comprehensive benefits package including health, dental, and vision benefits, sick and vacation days, and participation in the State Universities Retirement System. About NEIU Founded in 1867, Northeastern Illinois University enrolls about 5,500 students through the College of Arts and Sciences, the Daniel L. Goodwin College of Education, the College of Business and Technology and the College of Graduate Studies and Research. Northeastern is regarded as the most diverse public comprehensive university in the Midwest and is designated by the U.S. Department of Education as a Hispanic-Serving Institution. NEIU offers more than 40 undergraduate degree and certificate programs and more than 50 graduate degree, certificate, licensure and endorsement programs. NEIU’s Main Campus is located on 67 acres in a residential area on the Northwest Side of Chicago. The University has three additional locations in the metropolitan area: the Jacob H. Carruthers Center for Inner City Studies, El Centro and the Center for College Access and Success. NEIU also is a founding member of the University Center of Lake County consortium campus in suburban Lake County, north of Chicago. Read more about us at www.neiu.edu. Northeastern Illinois University welcomes candidates who will support our diverse and inclusive student community. NEIU is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer and invites applications from Women, Minorities, Veterans and Persons with Disabilities, as well as Other Qualified Individuals. Our Mission is You Request Information Plan a Visit Apply Now Footer Menu 1 Footer Menu 1 Online Learning Academic Calendar NEIUPort Maps & Directions Housing Events Employment Directory Community Library Main Campus 5500 North St. Louis Avenue Chicago, IL 60625 (773) 583-4050 Carruthers Center 700 East Oakwood Blvd. Chicago, IL 60625 (773) 268-7500 El Centro 3390 North Avondale Ave. Chicago, IL 60618 (773) 442-4080 University Center 1200 University Center Drive, Room 220B Grayslake, IL 60030 (847) 665-4000 Footer bottom Footer bottom Take a Virtual Tour Give to NEIU © 2022 Northeastern Illinois University | Legal | Login Also of Interest High-Quality Access-Driven Online Credit Courses Student Services and Support in Illinois University Campus Virtual Tour ↑"
